    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        51.27950668334961,
        252.26992797851562,
        408.1839904785156,
        261.2699279785156
      ],
      "text": "Molecular epidemiology, if used in a population-based manner over several years, can be highly",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        51.0095100402832,
        264.2669372558594,
        408.1021728515625,
        273.2669372558594
      ],
      "text": "sensitive for measuring the effectiveness of control programmes in general and for evaluating",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        50.92850875854492,
        276.2639465332031,
        408.4984436035156,
        285.2639465332031
      ],
      "text": "the effectiveness of contact investigation in reducing the incidence of TB in particular (27,28).",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        50.955509185791016,
        288.2609558105469,
        408.0932922363281,
        297.2789611816406
      ],
      "text": "Any case in a cluster (with an identical genotype) that is likely to be secondary to an identiﬁed",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        50.91950607299805,
        300.2759704589844,
        407.8862609863281,
        309.2759704589844
      ],
      "text": "index case represents a failure of the programme. The questions that should be asked are",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        50.72150802612305,
        312.26983642578125,
        407.8827819824219,
        321.2729797363281
      ],
      "text": "“Why was this person not identiﬁed as a contact at the time of contact investigation?” and, if",
      "font": "TheSansSemiLight-Plain",
